\section*{AP \({ }^{\text {® }}\) CALCULUS AB \\ 2010 SCORING GUIDELINES (Form B)}

\section*{Question 4}

A squirrel starts at building \(A\) at time \(t=0\) and travels along a straight wire connected to building \(B\). For \(0 \leq t \leq 18\), the squirrel's velocity is modeled by the piecewise-linear function defined by the graph above.
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] At what times in the interval \(0<t<18\), if any, does the squirrel change direction? Give a reason for your answer.
\item[(b)] At what time in the interval \(0 \leq t \leq 18\) is the squirrel farthest from building \(A\) ? How far from building \(A\) is the squirrel at this time?
\end{itemize}
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/cb2e48b9-150c-4214-acc1-6f37f0f51637-1.jpg?height=370&width=748&top_left_y=412&top_left_x=1197)
\begin{itemize}
\item[(c)] Find the total distance the squirrel travels during the time interval \(0 \leq t \leq 18\).
\item[(d)] Write expressions for the squirrel's acceleration \(a(t)\), velocity \(v(t)\), and distance \(x(t)\) from building \(A\) that are valid for the time interval \(7<t<10\).
\item[(a)] The squirrel changes direction whenever its velocity changes sign. This occurs at \(t=9\) and \(t=15\).
\item[(b)] Velocity is 0 at \(t=0, t=9\), and \(t=15\).
\end{itemize}

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|}
\hline \(t\) & position at time \(t\) \\
\hline 0 & 0 \\
\hline 9 & \(\frac{9+5}{2} \cdot 20=140\) \\
\hline 15 & \(140-\frac{6+4}{2} \cdot 10=90\) \\
\hline 18 & \(90+\frac{3+2}{2} \cdot 10=115\) \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
The squirrel is farthest from building \(A\) at time \(t=9\); its greatest distance from the building is 140.
\begin{itemize}
\item[(c)] The total distance traveled is \(\int_{0}^{18}|v(t)| d t=140+50+25=215\).
\item[(d)] For \(7<t<10, a(t)=\frac{20-(-10)}{7-10}=-10\)
\[
\begin{aligned}
v(t) & =20-10(t-7)=-10 t+90 \\
x(7) & =\frac{7+5}{2} \cdot 20=120 \\
x(t) & =x(7)+\int_{7}^{t}(-10 u+90) d u \\
& =120+\left.\left(-5 u^{2}+90 u\right)\right|_{u=7} ^{u=t} \\
& =-5 t^{2}+90 t-265
\end{aligned}
\]
